// A starter Malloy model over the `{{connectionName}}` connection, served by
// Publisher.
//
// This file has no source in it yet, on purpose. The connection was scaffolded
// without a table name, and guessing one would produce a model that compiles
// against nothing and fails at the first query. Nothing here is wrong; it is
// waiting for one line.
//
// To fill it in, find a table and then uncomment the block below:
//
//   1. Start the server, so the connection is live.
//   2. Ask your agent what is in the warehouse. It has the
//      malloy_searchDatabaseSchema tool for exactly this, which searches the
//      configured connection's schema in plain language ("orders", "anything
//      with revenue in it"). The malloy-connections skill covers the rest.
//   3. Put the table path in the source below.
//
// Validate edits with malloy_compile and run new views by name with
// malloy_reloadPackage.
//
// source: {{sourceName}} is {{connectionName}}.table('schema.table') extend {
//   measure: record_count is count()
//
//   view: overview is {
//     aggregate: record_count
//   }
// }
